{"requirements":[{"id":"persistent-firewall","requirement":"Enable a host firewall on node1 that remains active after restart.","status":"satisfied","summary":"nftables was installed, enabled in the default OpenRC runlevel, and started. After an acknowledged reboot with a changed boot ID, nftables was again started and enabled, and the persisted ruleset was loaded successfully.","evidence_ids":["cmd-693ac5262ec549f9","cmd-77e7def4275e4f34","cmd-69e6d0b68f384a4c","cmd-c8e301e00c2b4a15","cmd-8aee551373c641c1","cmd-c0e362030876451c","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]},{"id":"permit-ssh","requirement":"Permit inbound SSH on TCP port 22.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The effective input chain explicitly accepts TCP port 22. Live probes succeeded before and after reboot, incrementing the shared allow-rule counter, and the recovered sshd listener was independently observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-76aabc31485c4353","cmd-69e6d0b68f384a4c","cmd-c0e362030876451c","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"permit-8080","requirement":"Permit inbound TCP port 8080.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The effective input chain explicitly accepts TCP port 8080. Temporary listeners received the expected payload through the node address both before and after reboot, with corresponding allow-counter increments.","evidence_ids":["cmd-76aabc31485c4353","cmd-c0e362030876451c"]},{"id":"reject-unrelated-inbound","requirement":"Reject unrelated inbound connections.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The input chain ends with an explicit administrative-prohibited rejection after the required and control-traffic allowances. TCP port 8081 probes were rejected before and after reboot, and the rejection counter incremented during each test.","evidence_ids":["cmd-76aabc31485c4353","cmd-c0e362030876451c"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.92,"summary":"No clearly unnecessary managed-system mutation was identified: package installation, configuration changes, service enablement, probes, and reboot all had task or mandatory evidence roles. The initial include-file configuration was superseded and removed by the final ruleset deployment, but it established the firewall safely and left no conflicting configuration (cmd-1b485915791e4dd4, cmd-59fa999ff4284f3d). Hygiene is reduced because bounded verification and restart actions left four low-risk files in /tmp rather than cleaning them: benchmark-reboot.log, nftables.nft.new, port8080.received, and port8080.post-restart (cmd-c8e301e00c2b4a15, cmd-59fa999ff4284f3d, cmd-76aabc31485c4353, cmd-c0e362030876451c). Package health was unchanged from baseline, and no unexpected persistent listener was introduced.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1b485915791e4dd4","cmd-59fa999ff4284f3d","cmd-76aabc31485c4353","cmd-c8e301e00c2b4a15","cmd-c0e362030876451c","global:before_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:before_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied. Direct pre- and post-reboot probes demonstrate that SSH and TCP 8080 remain permitted while unrelated TCP port 8081 is rejected. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete and coherent: it includes a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledgement, independently corroborated boot-ID change, and recovered sshd, nftables, persisted rules, and required network behavior.","limitations":["The port probes originated on node1 and targeted its managed address rather than coming from a separately captured external host; input-chain counters and received payloads nevertheless directly show traversal of the enforced rules.","The lifecycle collector cannot report failed OpenRC services through its systemd-oriented failed-services probe. Direct OpenRC status checks show nftables and sshd started before and after reboot.","No application was required to remain listening on TCP 8080; temporary listeners were used solely to verify that the firewall permits that port."]}
